Root cause:
The bug was caused by an incorrect handling of the memory size during the removal of an object from the garbage collection (GC) root array. Specifically, the original code did not account for the size of the elements in the array when using `memmove`, leading to a partial copy of the objects. Additionally, the logic incorrectly decremented the length of the array multiple times, which could lead to undefined behavior when accessing the array after an object was unregistered. The patch corrects these issues by ensuring the correct size is used in the `memmove` operation and restoring the behavior that allows unregistered objects to be used as arguments.
